    {
      "id": "graph-contract-overview",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Overview",
      "position": {
        "x": 740,
        "y": -180
      },
      "width": 660,
      "height": 380,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Ratified Invariant Core\n\nA `.node` artifact becomes a **graph** when it contains one authority-bearing **declaration** node and one canonical declared `root` surface.\n\nThe root is the graph's stable routing boundary and normal entry. `data.declaration.defaultSurfaceId` must be `root`, and the declared root must resolve to a real graph-owned port. The root may own its presentation or explicitly delegate to another graph-owned view; it does not prescribe one universal card design.\n\nLayer 1 requires:\n- one canonical declaration with stable graph identity\n- one declared `root` surface backed by a real `port`\n- every target promised by that surface, and every authored named handle, to exist\n- explicit authority through real `bridge` primitives for non-native node and edge classes\n- ports to expose graph-owned surfaces and portals to consume external surfaces; neither impersonates a bridge\n- durable cross-graph references and explicit source ownership\n- `dependencies.nodeTypes` that describe the graph's actual vocabulary\n\nThese are executable validity rules. Validators report broken declarations and broken promises; they do not report the absence of optional decoration, semantic edges, or unclaimed capabilities.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n`manifest` remains readable as compatibility data but should not be created by new templates. Compatibility behavior must be reported separately from invariant-core errors.\n\n## Analytics Is Not Graph-ness\n\n`data.analytics` is optional policy metadata. It does not determine graph validity, saveability, publication, or navigation. Measurement occurs only for a focused eligible graph view; preview, embed, bridge, class-resolution, and background loads are not graph page views.",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "markdown",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node"
        },
        "_bridge": {
          "classKey": "markdown",
          "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node"
        },
        "definitionKey": "markdown"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "graph-contract-shape",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Minimum Shape",
      "position": {
        "x": 740,
        "y": 250
      },
      "width": 400,
      "height": 460,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Minimum Shape\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"declaration\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"identity\": { \"graphId\": \"stable-id\" },\n    \"intent\": { \"kind\": \"graph\" },\n    \"authority\": {},\n    \"dependencies\": { \"nodeTypes\": [\"declaration\", \"port\"] },\n    \"declaresKind\": \"graph\",\n    \"declaration\": {\n      \"kind\": \"graph\",\n      \"targetMode\": \"artifact\",\n      \"artifactKind\": \"graph\",\n      \"defaultSurfaceId\": \"root\",\n      \"surfaces\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"kind\": \"port\",\n          \"portNodeId\": \"root-port-node-id\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe referenced root port must exist. If it delegates presentation to another graph-owned node, that promised target must exist too. Additional named surfaces remain subject to their family profile and exposure policy.\n\n## Reading Rule\n\nInterpret the declaration first, enter through its canonical root, then resolve additional surfaces or class authority explicitly.",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "markdown",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node"
        },
        "_bridge": {
          "classKey": "markdown",
          "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node"
        },
        "definitionKey": "markdown"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "graph-contract-conformance-layers",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Conformance Layers",
      "position": {
        "x": 1460,
        "y": -180
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 380,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Three Conformance Layers\n\n## Layer 1 — Invariant Core\nUniversal and executable. Failure means the artifact is ambiguous, unresolved, or structurally invalid as a Twilite graph.\n\n## Layer 2 — Family Profiles\nExecutable only for capabilities the graph explicitly claims. A declared surface that cannot resolve is a violation; an optional surface that was never promised is silent.\n\n## Layer 3 — Composition Law\nAdvisory organization patterns for semantic edges, sections, density, summaries, splitting, navigation, and visual layout. Templates and new-file generators should provide strong defaults, but missing composition is not a validator warning.\n\nDiagnostics report broken promises. Compatibility notes explain legacy behavior. Composition guidance belongs in templates, documentation, and deliberate review—not in an ever-growing warning queue.",
        "definitionKey": "markdown"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "graph-contract-template-boundary",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Template Boundary",
      "position": {
        "x": 1460,
        "y": 250
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 460,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Template Boundary\n\nA template is a graph with extra authoring intent and useful generated structure.\n\nDo not use template richness to decide whether another file is a valid graph. New-file generators may create structural edges such as `default surface`, `exposes`, `exports`, and `class authority`; editors may maintain relationships they own. Users are not required to retrofit those edges into older valid files.\n\nSemantic edges remain authored meaning. Templates should encourage them, especially in idea and edge-class graphs, but their absence is not a conformance failure.\n\nThe correct order is:\n1. establish base graph validity\n2. evaluate only capabilities the graph claims\n3. apply template guidance to new work and voluntary repair\n\nStandards protect execution. Templates encourage expression.",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "markdown",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node"
        },
        "_bridge": {
          "classKey": "markdown",
          "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node"
        },
        "definitionKey": "markdown"
      }
    }
  ],
